      "assistant_text": "According to [[write-journal]], the Guarded Write Journal page describes a mechanism that records the prior state of files before they are overwritten by the guarded tool executor. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: The journal captures each file\u0027s previous content (or records that the file didn\u0027t exist) before any write operation. If the agent run fails for any reason\u2014such as hitting a turn cap, encountering an unrecoverable error, or having writes denied\u2014the journal can roll back all writes in reverse order.\n\n**Key features**:\n- Restores previous content for files that existed before\n- Deletes files that were newly created during the run\n- Provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction\n- The journal itself acts as an in-memory transaction log, stored only for the duration of one run\n\n**Scope**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t actually use the rollback functionality since it has no write capability, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library for any agent that does write.",
